        "## 2. Why pandas?\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose a college stores student marks:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "85, 91, 76, 88\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "A Python list can store these values easily.\n",
        "\n",
        "But in data analysis, we often want more information attached to the values:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "Student     Marks\n",
        "Aarav       85\n",
        "Diya        91\n",
        "Kabir       76\n",
        "Meera       88\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Pandas allows us to work with the values **and** their labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "The two structures you will use most often are:\n",
        "\n",
        "### Series\n",
        "A one-dimensional labelled structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "### DataFrame\n",
        "A two-dimensional labelled structure, similar to a table.\n",
        "\n",
        "The **Index** provides labels that help pandas identify and align data."
      ],
      "id": "U_rBsrfGjSxg"
