        "# Part D – Index\n",
        "\n",
        "## 29. What is an Index?\n",
        "\n",
        "The index identifies the rows of a pandas object.\n",
        "\n",
        "If a DataFrame is displayed as:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "   Name    Marks\n",
        "0  Aarav   85\n",
        "1  Diya    91\n",
        "2  Kabir   76\n",
        "3  Meera   88\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "then `0, 1, 2, 3` form the row index.\n",
        "\n",
        "The index can also contain meaningful labels such as:\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "E101\n",
        "E102\n",
        "E103\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Indexes are important because pandas uses them for:\n",
        "\n",
        "- selecting rows\n",
        "- identifying records\n",
        "- aligning labelled data"
      ],
      "id": "aGrYKHDFjSxx"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "B3JQrmIHjSxx"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 30. Creating a DataFrame with a meaningful index\n",
        "\n",
        "A DataFrame can be created with an index from the beginning.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Live coding\n",
        "\n",
        "Create `employee_sales` with:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Employee: Riya, Arjun, Neha\n",
        "- Sales: 125000, 98000, 143000\n",
        "\n",
        "Use:\n",
        "\n",
        "`E101, E102, E103`\n",
        "\n",
        "as the row labels."
